& [SJS]
  + Situation: exact checkpoint custody exists but a host or model tool caller has no single typed request-response language over it
  + Justification: a closed operation union makes the attention-procedure boundary testable while separating compact inspection full host resolution and deterministic resume
  + Solution: dispatch four strict operations over a supplied registry and expose the scripted fixture through bounded stdin and stdout

& [Delineation]
  + query dispatch is a pure library transform and not an operating service
  + CLI stdin parsing is a local adapter and not provider tool-call wiring
  + inspect deliberately withholds full checkpoint and transport bodies
  + resolve is host-facing and deliberately returns exact full custody
  + resume computes existing fixture transitions and performs no model or external execution

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + request digest binds strict typed request
  + expected registry root provides caller-selected snapshot binding
  + operation union makes invalid input combinations unrepresentable after strict deserialization
  + response digest commits operation request digest registry root and result
  + bounded stdin prevents unbounded command ingestion

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty distinguishes inspection resolution resume provider execution and external effects
  + Security validates registry root exact handle request-response digests and closed operation variants
  + Planner gives each operation explicit required inputs and output type
  + Weaver joins one command surface to custody and canonical resume primitives
  + Scribe makes each request result and binding inspectable in strict JSON
  + Refiner keeps inspect output compact while reserving full state for explicit resolve
  + Observer compares protocol responses to the direct functions they expose

& [Decision]
  + activate isolated custody_query forms validation dispatch serializer bounded stdin command and adversarial tests
  + keep persistent custody live provider integration service concurrency and external effects outside authority

& [Rollback]
  + additive module CLI branch exports and tests remove without changing predecessor behavior
